v5-3.display:
Hear, O kings; give ear, you mighty satraps!
I will sing to the Lord;
I will make music to the God of Israel.

v5-7.display:
Phrazōn ceased in Israel;
it ceased until Deborah arose,
because a mother arose in Israel.

v5-19.display:
Kings came and drew up in battle;
then Canaan’s kings fought at Taanach by Megiddo’s water.
They took no greedy gain of silver.

v5-27.display:
Between her feet he bent down and fell;
he lay between her feet.
Where he bent down, there he fell, wretched.
